# scripts/.preamble-grandfather — preamble-ratchet allowlist (age-gate-the-ungated-egwt.10)
#
# Every top-level scripts/*.sh that did NOT source scripts/lib/preamble.sh at
# the ratchet cutoff. These pre-existing scripts are EXEMPT from the adoption
# requirement so the gate causes ZERO churn of the existing tree.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY: this allowlist only shrinks. When a grandfathered script adopts
# scripts/lib/preamble.sh, its line MUST be pruned here (the gate FAILS until
# it is). New scripts added after the cutoff are NOT added here — they must
# source the preamble or carry a '# preamble-exempt: <reason>' line.
#
# Regenerated at LAND time (after the final rebase) so it reflects the tree we
# actually land on. Generation command:
#   for f in scripts/*.sh; do grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*(\.|source)[[:space:]]+.*lib/preamble\.sh' "$f" || echo "$f"; done | LC_ALL=C sort
#
